flowchart TB
    accTitle: How a run tells new metadata from new content
    accDescr: A document that was never exported is downloaded. For an exported document, a run compares the revision of Paperless with the one it saved. With a new revision, it takes the checksum of the file that it kept for this revision, or asks Paperless for it, MD5 up to Paperless-ngx 2.x and SHA-256 since 3.0, and keeps it with the revision, so that a document that waits for a later run asks only once; it looks for the checksum among the SHA-256 and the MD5 that it saved at the download. When the revision is the same, or the checksum is among them, the content is the same: the file stays where it is, or moves to its new path. When an earlier version of the app saved the SHA-256 alone and Paperless reports an MD5, the run computes both checksums of the mirrored file: when its SHA-256 is the saved one and its MD5 the one of Paperless, the content is the same too. Otherwise the run downloads the document to a temporary file, computes both checksums in one pass over it, writes it to Nextcloud in chunks, into the file of the document when it has one, which keeps its ID and moves to its new path first, and saves the checksums. The questions are indigo, the requests to Paperless-ngx green, and the results in Nextcloud blue.

    document["A document that<br>Paperless lists"] --> exported{"Exported<br>before?"}
    exported -->|no| download["Download to a<br>temporary file, SHA-256<br>and MD5 in one pass"]
    exported -->|yes| revision{"Same revision<br>as saved?"}
    revision -->|yes| same["Same content"]
    revision -->|no| checksum["Checksum of the revision,<br>kept or from Paperless:<br>MD5 up to 2.x,<br>SHA-256 since 3.0"]
    checksum --> known{"Among the saved<br>SHA-256 and MD5?"}
    known -->|yes| same
    known -->|no| earlier{"Only the SHA-256 of<br>an earlier version? Is it<br>the mirrored file's, and<br>its MD5 Paperless's?"}
    earlier -->|yes| same
    earlier -->|no| download
    same --> path{"Same path?"}
    path -->|yes| unchanged["UNCHANGED"]
    path -->|no| move["MOVE: the same file<br>at its new path"]
    download --> export["EXPORT: written in chunks<br>into the same file, or<br>a new one; both<br>checksums saved"]
    classDef check fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef paperless fill:#17803d2e,stroke:#17803d,stroke-width:2px
    classDef nextcloud fill:#0082c92e,stroke:#0082c9,stroke-width:2px
    class exported,revision,known,earlier,path check
    class checksum,download paperless
    class unchanged,move,export nextcloud
